# probe-service

This is a lightweight POC AI-fication repo. Read [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) before making changes.

## Structure

- Normal Java Spring Boot service under `com.codeistari.probe`
- Packages: `controller`, `dto`, `service`, `client`, `mapper`, `config`, `exception`, `domain`
- Do not structure the codebase around `forge-service`; it is a downstream dependency only

## DTO boundaries

- Public API DTOs: `dto/request`, `dto/response` (Probe* naming)
- Downstream forge REST DTOs: `dto/client/forge/` (Forge* naming)
- Do not reuse public API DTOs as downstream REST DTOs

## Contracts

- Do not change the `forge-service` REST/gRPC contract from probe-service
- Proto source of truth: `proto/artifact_forge_service.proto`

## AI-fication baseline

Full AI-fication baseline is installed (`docs/architecture.md`, `docs/entities-enums.md`, `docs/external-services.md`, `docs/flows/`, Parallel SDD adapters). Keep them accurate but proportionally small — see "Parallel SDD" in `AGENTS.md`.

## Parallel SDD

Spec Kit (`.sdd-parallel/adapters/spec-kit/`, natively registered under `.specify/extensions/parallel-sdd/`) and OpenSpec (`openspec/schemas/myntra-sdd/`) are both installed and ready/activated. Before planning or implementing a feature driven through either framework: read its `status.yaml` and review reports, run Gate 1 (design-check) before planning and Gate 2 (implementation-check) before implementing per `.sdd-parallel/WORKFLOW.md`, and use `[SDD-TECH][<initiative-id>]` / `[SDD-IMPL][<initiative-id>]` PR title prefixes. Never infer `implemented` from similar code or without merged-PR/test/doc evidence. See the full "Parallel SDD" section in `AGENTS.md`.
